# CASM Phase 12 WP72 trusted reference: casmzpconst1
#
# Independently hand-assembled from the casmzpconst1 fixture source in
# cmake/GenerateCasmTestFixtures.cmake. NOT produced by CASM. Proves the
# WP72 fix directly: a named constant (equate) whose resolved value is in
# zero-page range ($00-$FF) must select zero-page (2-byte) addressing for
# STA, exactly like a bare numeric literal operand already does -- not
# absolute (3-byte) addressing, which is what CASM produced before this
# fix. Mirrors WP71's own real-world discovery site verbatim (DASH's
# dmain.s: STA DISPATCHVECTOR / STA DISPATCHVECTOR+1, DISPATCHVECTOR = $70).
#
# Source (.ORG $C000):
#   DISPATCHVECTOR = $70
#   STA DISPATCHVECTOR
#   STA DISPATCHVECTOR+1
#
# Hand assembly:
#   00 C0        PRG load-address header ($C000, little-endian)
#   85 70        STA $70   (zero-page, 2 bytes -- NOT 8D 70 00 absolute)
#   85 71        STA $71   (zero-page, 2 bytes -- NOT 8D 71 00 absolute)
#
# bytes: 6
# sha256: d31bc5e4c23e08c9af8c69034c689347293766fd2df1c77bb14157a2a306d821
# source_sha256: casmzpconst1.seq=6750352d5923dbe6fb018c9862c9c9ba6cae9852b2b254be62c567fc947d14b6
